<h2 data-start=3D"6373" data-end=3D"6451" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6376" data-end=3D"6451">4. Relation Many-to-Many (Plusieurs =C3=A0 Plusieur=
s) avec <code data-start=3D"6432" data-end=3D"6449">ManyToManyField</code><=
/strong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"6453" data-end=3D"6737" class=3D"">La relation <strong dat=
a-start=3D"6465" data-end=3D"6481">Many-to-Many</strong> est utilis=C3=A9e =
lorsqu'un mod=C3=A8le peut =C3=AAtre li=C3=A9 =C3=A0 plusieurs instances d=
=E2=80=99un autre mod=C3=A8le et inversement. Par exemple, une relation ent=
re <strong data-start=3D"6614" data-end=3D"6627">=C3=A9tudiants</strong> et=
 <strong data-start=3D"6631" data-end=3D"6640">cours</strong> o=C3=B9 un =
=C3=A9tudiant peut suivre plusieurs cours, et un cours peut =C3=AAtre suivi=
 par plusieurs =C3=A9tudiants.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"6739" data-end=3D"6787" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6743" data-end=3D"6787">4.1. D=C3=A9finition d=E2=80=99un Mod=C3=A8le Many-=
to-Many</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"6789" data-end=3D"6869" class=3D"">Voici un exemple de rel=
ation <strong data-start=3D"6818" data-end=3D"6834">Many-to-Many</strong> e=
ntre des =C3=A9tudiants et des cours :</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"6871" data-end=3D"6885" class=3D"">Exemple :</h4>
<pre class=3D"!overflow-visible" data-start=3D"6887" data-end=3D"7123"><div=
