<h2 data-start=3D"2508" data-end=3D"2548" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2511" data-end=3D"2548">1. Introduction aux Microservices</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"2550" data-end=3D"2593" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2554" data-end=3D"2593">1.1. Qu'est-ce qu'un microservice ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2595" data-end=3D"2865" class=3D"">Un microservice est une=
 unit=C3=A9 de travail ind=C3=A9pendante qui se concentre sur une fonction =
m=C3=A9tier sp=C3=A9cifique d'une application. Chaque microservice est une =
application autonome qui peut =C3=AAtre d=C3=A9ploy=C3=A9e, mise =C3=A0 l'=
=C3=A9chelle et mise =C3=A0 jour ind=C3=A9pendamment des autres microservic=
es.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2867" data-end=3D"2907" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2871" data-end=3D"2907">1.2. Avantages des microservices</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2909" data-end=3D"3302">
<li data-start=3D"2909" data-end=3D"2985" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2911" data-end=3D"2985" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
911" data-end=3D"2926">=C3=89volutivit=C3=A9</strong> : Chaque service peut=
 =C3=AAtre mis =C3=A0 l'=C3=A9chelle ind=C3=A9pendamment.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2986" data-end=3D"3083" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2988" data-end=3D"3083" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
988" data-end=3D"3002">R=C3=A9silience</strong> : Si un microservice =C3=A9=
choue, l=E2=80=99ensemble du syst=C3=A8me peut continuer =C3=A0 fonctionner=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3084" data-end=3D"3190" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3086" data-end=3D"3190" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
086" data-end=3D"3113">Facilit=C3=A9 de d=C3=A9ploiement</strong> : Les mic=
roservices peuvent =C3=AAtre d=C3=A9ploy=C3=A9s ind=C3=A9pendamment les uns=
 des autres.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3191" data-end=3D"3302" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3193" data-end=3D"3302" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
193" data-end=3D"3223">Technologies ind=C3=A9pendantes</strong> : Chaque se=
rvice peut utiliser des technologies diff=C3=A9rentes selon ses besoins.</p=
>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"3304" data-end=3D"3359" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3308" data-end=3D"3359">1.3. Architecture microservices vs monolithique</st=
rong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"3361" data-end=3D"3723">
<li data-start=3D"3361" data-end=3D"3535" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3363" data-end=3D"3535" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
363" data-end=3D"3392">Architecture Monolithique</strong> : L'ensemble de l=
'application est d=C3=A9ploy=C3=A9 comme une seule unit=C3=A9, ce qui peut =
devenir difficile =C3=A0 maintenir =C3=A0 mesure que l=E2=80=99application =
grandit.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3536" data-end=3D"3723" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3538" data-end=3D"3723" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
538" data-end=3D"3568">Architecture Microservices</strong> : Chaque fonctio=
nnalit=C3=A9 est divis=C3=A9e en petits services autonomes, chacun ayant sa=
 propre base de donn=C3=A9es, son cycle de vie et son =C3=A9quipe de d=C3=
=A9veloppement.</p>
</li>
</ul>
